+## R5 Mid-Flash — DOM identity fix
+
+### Defect (verified 2026-07-28)
+
+Cypress acceptance suite reports 4 detached-DOM failures on toggle/toggle-all/clear-completed.
+Root cause: `render()` in `js/app.js` calls `todoListEl.innerHTML = ''` and rebuilds every
+`<li>` element, destroying DOM node identity. In-harness (happy-dom) re-queries the DOM and
+passes; a real browser holds a detached reference and fails.
+
+### Spec work done
+
+- `assets/dom-identity-scantling.md` — mechanical shape specifying element preservation
+- `assets/scantling-register.json` — registration
+- `toggle-todos.feature` — 4 new `@contract @planks(render seam)` scenarios referencing the scantling
+- `watchbill.json` — 6 watches (replaced previous 8), including conformance checker + fix
+- `RIGGING.md` — added `assets` and `scantlings` directories, `conformance` command
+
+### Watchbill dispatch order
+
+1-4: Existing feature scenarios (pass on current code)
+5: Bespoke conformance checker implementation (step definitions for contract scenarios)
+6: Production fix (mutate in place, remove `innerHTML = ''` on todoListEl)
+
+### Verdict for QM
+
+Watch 5 scenarios fail on current code because no step definitions exist. After Crew
+implements the checker in watch 5, scenarios fail because the current source violates the
+scantling (uses `innerHTML = ''`). After watch 6 fix, all scenarios pass.
