+# DOM Element Identity Scantling
+
+## Purpose
+
+The `render()` function in `js/app.js` MUST preserve existing `<li>` elements in the
+`.todo-list` when a todo's completed state changes.  A real browser holds references
+to DOM nodes across interaction chains; replacing a node destroys the reference and
+causes detached-DOM failures in acceptance suites.
+
+This scantling specifies the mechanical constraint on the `render` seam.
+
+## Definition
+
+**DOM element identity** — when the application mutates a todo's `completed` field in
+the model and calls `render()`, every `<li>` element representing a todo that still
+exists in the filtered set MUST be the same `Element` object as it was before the
+call.  The element MAY have its CSS class, checkbox state, or text content modified,
+but the element node itself MUST NOT be removed and replaced.
+
+## Invariants
+
+| Context | Invariant |
+|---|---|
+| Individual toggle | After `toggleTodo(title)` → `render()`, the `<li>` whose `label.textContent` matches `title` is the same `Element` object as before the call. |
+| Toggle all (mark) | After `toggleAll(true)` → `render()`, every `<li>` present before the call is the same `Element` object after the call, and all have class `completed`. |
+| Toggle all (clear) | After `toggleAll(false)` → `render()`, every `<li>` present before the call is the same `Element` object after the call, and none have class `completed`. |
+| Clear completed | After `clearCompleted()` → `render()`, every `<li>` for a non-completed todo that existed before the call is the same `Element` object after the call.  Completed-todo `<li>` elements MAY be removed. |
+
+## Prohibited patterns
+
+The `render()` function MUST NOT contain any of:
+
+- `innerHTML = ''` or `innerHTML =` assignment on `todoListEl` or any ancestor of
+  a `<li>` element whose content is the todo list
+- `replaceChildren()` on `todoListEl`
+- `removeChild()` in a loop that removes and re-appends all children
+- Any operation that detaches all children of `todoListEl` and recreates them
+
+Allowed: `classList.add/remove/toggle`, `setAttribute`, `.checked =`, `.textContent =`,
+`.style.* =` on individual `<li>` elements or their descendants.
+
+## Enforcement
+
+A source-level conformance checker (bespoke, Crew-implemented) scans `js/app.js` for
+the prohibited patterns within the `render()` function and reports a counterexample
+if any is found.  The `@contract` scenarios in `toggle-todos.feature` rely on this
+checker; they are tagged `@planks(render seam)` so the plank inventory can track them.
\ No newline at end of file
